    "summary": "Wood drum (used in dance) with lizard skin (?) membrane, hour-glass shaped, with handle. Lower third decorated with low-relief carving and European paint: three motifs of concentric circles, below them three green tear-drop motifs, above them a band of chevrons some of which are painted green, traces of red paint on others. Green band at the base. Inscribed near the handle &quot;Kai.Tupi&quot;. With detached cane coil which originally held the membrane in place.",
